# netsurf: HTML's hiding rules ([hidden], dialog, template, details) + summary toggle
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 76e8c77 (patch stack through 202)
#
# The UA stylesheet (resources/default.css) predates HTML5's rendering
# section: nothing hid an element with the `hidden` attribute, a closed
# <dialog>, a <template>, <datalist>, or the body of a closed <details>.
# Every page that keeps markup hidden until a script reveals it -- cookie
# banners, menus, modals, tab panels, "read more" sections, error
# messages, Wikipedia's collapsed sections -- showed all of it at once.
#
# Fix:
#  - default.css: [hidden], template, datalist, dialog, source, track,
#    param, area { display: none } (UA origin, so an author `display`
#    still wins, as in every browser); dialog[open] shows as an absolutely
#    positioned, horizontally centred, fit-content box with a border and
#    1em padding; details and summary are blocks; a closed details hides
#    every element child but its summaries; the first summary gets a
#    disclosure triangle (U+25B8 closed, U+25BE open).
#  - vita_polyfill.js: hiding a details body is only safe if it can be
#    opened, so a click on a details element's first summary toggles its
#    `open` attribute as the activation behaviour (a window-level click
#    listener; preventDefault cancels it; once per event) and queues a
#    non-bubbling `toggle`. details.open / dialog.open reflect the
#    attribute; dialog.show() / showModal() open it; close(v) closes it,
#    sets returnValue and queues `close`.
# Boundaries: showModal() does not make the rest of the page inert or put
# the dialog in a top layer (it opens like show()); no ::backdrop; a bare
# text node directly inside a closed details stays visible (CSS cannot
# select text nodes); [hidden=until-found] is treated as plain hidden.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/HTML-hidden-details.html (HIDDEN203, 9 checks,
# Chromium 9/9; 0/9 without the patch). Full gate: see
# docs/build-loop-state.md.
